  "details": "With the release of the avatar marketplace I'm sure there will be options for players to change things like colors or styles to make the avatar truly theirs without needing to use unity or blender. Though when you reset your avatar it will cause you to have to redo those settings. \n\nWhat about a button in the \"quick action\" menu that would \"save avatar state\". The idea of this would be to save an instance of the avatar with the parameters at their current settings so a player can effectively reset their avatar while also keeping their custom settings. While still leaving the full reset available if for some reason the player wants to reset their save state back to default.\n\nThis would also have a usage for assets like Liindy's \"Otherwordly Fishing Rod\" which is effectively a game added to your avatar. You could also use the state to save progress, making the state system have multiple use cases for both more low to the ground \"marketplace users\" and power users that add more advanced assets to their avatar.",
